<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  ForgottenArsenalAndUnboundHive.xml      Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  Builds FACTION_SPEC.md sections 13 and 14. Two label-only reskins, and they
  share a file because between them they are four operations.

    13 · the Forgotten Arsenal  ->  vanilla `Mechanoid`
    14 · the Unbound Hive       ->  vanilla `Insect`

  READ FROM THE SHIPPED DEFS, 2026-08-14 ; not inferred:
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Core\Defs\
    FactionDefs\Factions_Hidden.xml

      Mechanoid   ParentName FactionBase · label "mechanoid hive" ·
                  hidden true · permanentEnemy true · techLevel Ultra ·
                  factionNameMaker NamerFactionMechanoid ·
                  6 Combat pawnGroupMakers · NO settlementGenerationWeight node
      Insect      ParentName FactionBase · label "insect geneline" ·
                  hidden true · fixedName "Sorne Geneline" · techLevel Animal ·
                  permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept · 1 Combat pawnGroupMaker

  Both carry `label` and `description` on the def itself, so both are
  `Replace`, never `Add`.

  🔴 LABEL AND DESCRIPTION ONLY, ON PURPOSE.
  `hidden true` is CORRECT and stays: the Forgotten Arsenal is a what, not a
  who. It has no leader, no settlements and no diplomacy, and it never needed a
  `settlementGenerationWeight` node because it has none to begin with. The
  Unbound Hive gets the same treatment ; its name exists only to keep it apart
  from the Geonosian Foundry Hive, which is the AUTHORED insectoid faction.

  ⛔ Both inherit their `pawnGroupMakers` wholesale. Alpha Mechs and several
  other mods patch `Mechanoid`'s group makers directly, and every mechanoid
  raid on the map comes through them. Nothing here goes near that list.

  ⚠️ `Insect/fixedName` "Sorne Geneline" is deliberately left in place. The
  spec asks for a label change, and the fixed name is what the hive calls
  itself in-world.

  ⚠️ Neither faction takes an ideo. Sections 13 and 14 both say "none".

  SAFETY
  ======
  Each def gets its own conditional, so a missing or renamed vessel silences
  only its own half instead of taking the other down with it. Every defName
  written here is vanilla Core, so no `MayRequire` is owed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- 13 · the Forgotten Arsenal -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>the Forgotten Arsenal</label></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>Not a polity. A standing order that outlived the people who gave it, and the machines that are still carrying it out.\n\nThey wake in buried structures, under drift and under salt, and they resume. Nobody negotiates with the Arsenal because there is nothing there to negotiate with.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- 14 · the Unbound Hive -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Insect"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Insect"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>the Unbound Hive</label></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Insect"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>Giant insectoids that live under the rock and come up through it when noise or scent tells them something soft is standing above.\n\nUnbound because nothing owns them — no foundry, no caste, no purpose but the tunnel and what is at the end of it.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
